{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1101","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"G. (Zero XOR Subset)-less"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You are given an array $$$a_1, a_2, \\dots, a_n$$$ of integer numbers."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Your task is to divide the array into the maximum number of segments in such a way that:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" each element is contained in "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"exactly one"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" segment; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" each segment contains at least one element; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" there doesn't exist a non-empty subset of segments such that bitwise XOR of the numbers from them is equal to $$$0$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Print the maximum number of segments the array can be divided into. Print "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"-1"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" if no suitable division exists."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains a single integer $$$n$$$ ($$$1 \\le n \\le 2 \\cdot 10^5$$$) — the size of the array."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The second line contains $$$n$$$ integers $$$a_1, a_2, \\dots, a_n$$$ ($$$0 \\le a_i \\le 10^9$$$)."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Print the maximum number of segments the array can be divided into while following the given constraints. Print "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"-1"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" if no suitable division exists."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n4\n5 5 7 2\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n2\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n3\n1 2 3\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n-1\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n3\n3 1 10\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n3\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first example $$$2$$$ is the maximum number. If you divide the array into $$$\\{[5], [5, 7, 2]\\}$$$, the XOR value of the subset of only the second segment is $$$5 \\oplus 7 \\oplus 2 = 0$$$. $$$\\{[5, 5], [7, 2]\\}$$$ has the value of the subset of only the first segment being $$$5 \\oplus 5 = 0$$$. However, $$$\\{[5, 5, 7], [2]\\}$$$ will lead to subsets $$$\\{[5, 5, 7]\\}$$$ of XOR $$$7$$$, $$$\\{[2]\\}$$$ of XOR $$$2$$$ and $$$\\{[5, 5, 7], [2]\\}$$$ of XOR $$$5 \\oplus 5 \\oplus 7 \\oplus 2 = 5$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Let's take a look at some division on $$$3$$$ segments — $$$\\{[5], [5, 7], [2]\\}$$$. It will produce subsets:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$\\{[5]\\}$$$, XOR $$$5$$$; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$\\{[5, 7]\\}$$$, XOR $$$2$$$; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$\\{[5], [5, 7]\\}$$$, XOR $$$7$$$; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$\\{[2]\\}$$$, XOR $$$2$$$; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$\\{[5], [2]\\}$$$, XOR $$$7$$$; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$\\{[5, 7], [2]\\}$$$, XOR $$$0$$$; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$\\{[5], [5, 7], [2]\\}$$$, XOR $$$5$$$; "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"As you can see, subset $$$\\{[5, 7], [2]\\}$$$ has its XOR equal to $$$0$$$, which is unacceptable. You can check that for other divisions of size $$$3$$$ or $$$4$$$, non-empty subset with $$$0$$$ XOR always exists."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The second example has no suitable divisions."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The third example array can be divided into $$$\\{[3], [1], [10]\\}$$$. No subset of these segments has its XOR equal to $$$0$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"G","problemCode":"1101G","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1101/problem/G"}